READ_ME {
Two things a program may not do with a library's type: use an operator the
library answers only for itself (`-` is `ratio.xag`'s alone), and answer an
operator for the type in its own unit (`mod`). Both are refused.
}
PREP {
    import 'ratio';
    fn.ra.ratio 'mod' [loan.ra.ratio 'a', loan.ra.ratio 'b'] { give [ra.over[*0*, *1*]]; }
}
START {
    print.stdout[ra.over[*1*, *2*] - ra.over[*1*, *3*] \n];
}
ITMT {
}
